---
/**
 * Privacy policy, English. Translation of /fr/confidentialite, which remains
 * the governing version.
 *
 * Every factual claim here has to stay true of the deployed site. The two
 * things that touch personal data are Vercel's server logs and the mailbox
 * behind hello@dupflo.dev; analytics is cookieless and aggregate.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { business, addressLine, formatDate } from '../config/business';
import { identityTwin } from '../i18n/pages';

const lang = 'en' as const;
const twin = identityTwin('privacy', lang);

const title = 'Privacy policy';
const description =
  'What personal data this site handles, why, for how long, and how to exercise your rights. No advertising cookie, no marketing tracker.';
---

<Base lang={lang} title={title} description={description} translationHref={twin}>
  <PageHeader
    title={title}
    intro="What this site knows about you, why, and how to have it erased."
  />

  <div class="prose mt-8">
    <p>
      This is an editorial site: it is read without an account and without a
      form. There is almost nothing for it to process. What follows states
      exactly what there is, and on what basis.
    </p>

    <h2>Data controller</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>{business.legalName}</strong>, {business.legalForm.en},
      SIRET {business.siret}, {addressLine()}.
      <br />
      For anything concerning personal data:
      {' '}<a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Given the nature and volume of the processing, appointing a data protection
      officer is not required. Requests are handled directly by the controller.
    </p>

    <h2>Data processed</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Host server logs.</strong> Every request to the site is logged by
        Vercel: IP address, timestamp, requested URL, response code, user agent,
        referrer. These logs are generated automatically by the infrastructure.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Contact messages.</strong> If you write to {business.email}, I
        process your email address, your name where the message carries one, and
        the content of the message.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Aggregate analytics.</strong> Vercel Analytics counts page views
        without a cookie, without a persistent identifier and without browser
        fingerprinting. The data is aggregate: I see volumes per page, not
        visitors.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Article reactions.</strong> The button at the end of an article
        increments a counter. It records no identity, no IP address, and nothing
        that ties that click to you.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>No advertising cookie, no marketing tracker, no social pixel, no
      data sold.</strong> The site sets no non-essential cookie, so there is no
      consent to collect and no banner to display.
    </p>
    <p>
      No special category of data within the meaning of Article 9 GDPR is
      collected, and the site is not directed at children under fifteen.
    </p>

    <h2>Purposes and legal bases</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Serving the pages and keeping the site secure</strong> (server
        logs): legitimate interest, Article 6(1)(f) GDPR. The interest pursued is
        keeping the site available and detecting abuse, such as an attack or a
        spike of automated traffic.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Answering a message</strong> (contact email): performance of a
        request you initiate, Article 6(1)(b) where it concerns an engagement,
        legitimate interest, Article 6(1)(f), otherwise.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Understanding which pages are read</strong> (cookieless aggregate
        analytics): legitimate interest, Article 6(1)(f), exempt from consent
        since nothing is stored on your device.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      No automated decision-making and no profiling is carried out on this data.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Contact messages: 12 months</strong> from the last exchange, then
        deleted. Exchanges that lead to a commercial relationship are kept under
        accounting and tax obligations, which is ten years for supporting
        documents.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Server logs: around 30 days</strong>, per the host's retention
        policy, then purged automatically.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Analytics: aggregate figures only</strong>, with no individual
        record to keep or erase.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Recipients</h2>
    <p>
      Your data is not sold, rented or handed on. It is accessible to me, and to
      the technical processors strictly needed to run the site:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>{business.host.name}</strong> ({business.host.address}):
        hosting, page delivery, server logs, analytics.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>My email provider</strong>: delivery and storage of the messages
        you send me.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Upstash</strong>: storage of the reaction counter, which holds no
        personal data.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Each acts on instruction, under a processing agreement within the meaning
      of Article 28 GDPR.
    </p>

    <h2>Transfers outside the European Union</h2>
    <p>
      {business.host.name} is a company incorporated in the United States. Some
      processing, the server logs in particular, may therefore involve a transfer
      of data outside the European Union.
    </p>
    <p>
      Those transfers are covered by the European Commission's
      <strong> standard contractual clauses</strong> (decision 2021/914),
      together with the host's technical measures: encryption in transit and at
      rest, and access partitioning. No data is transferred to a third country
      outside that framework.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under Articles 15 to 22 GDPR you have the right of access, rectification,
      erasure, restriction of processing, objection to processing based on
      legitimate interest, and data portability.
    </p>
    <p>
      To exercise any of them, write to
      {' '}<a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> or to
      {' '}{addressLine()}. You will get an answer within one month, extendable
      by two months for a complex request, in which case you will be told. Proof
      of identity may be requested where there is reasonable doubt about who is
      asking.
    </p>
    <p>
      If the answer does not satisfy you, you may lodge a complaint with the
      French data protection authority, the <strong>CNIL</strong>, 3 place de
      Fontenoy, TSA 80715, 75334 Paris Cedex 07, or online:
      {' '}<a href="https://www.cnil.fr/en/plaintes" rel="noopener" target="_blank">
        cnil.fr/en/plaintes
      </a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      The site is served over <strong>HTTPS</strong> only, with
      <strong> HSTS</strong>: a browser that has visited it once refuses any
      unencrypted connection afterwards. The usual security headers are in place,
      notably against framing the site from a third-party origin and against
      content-type sniffing.
    </p>
    <p>
      Pages are pre-rendered and served as static files: there is no visitor
      database, no user account and no session, so there are no credentials to
      protect. Access to the administration tools — code repository and hosting —
      is protected by two-factor authentication.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      This policy may be updated to follow changes in the site or in the
      regulation. The version in force is the one published on this page, dated
      below.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing version</h2>
    <p>
      This is a translation. The
      {' '}<a href={twin} hreflang="fr" lang="fr">French version</a> prevails in
      case of any discrepancy.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p class="mt-10 border-t pt-4 text-[12px] text-dim">
    Last updated: {formatDate(business.updatedAt, lang)}
  </p>
</Base>
